0459: StarbiteMali recycles its buffers.

S5a 2026-11-15 (macOS Sequoia at 2x, 300 s): "STARLTE GPU CALLS" summed over the run: 12192 GPU jobs in 9.7 s,
but 844 buffer creates in 36 s (43 ms each) and 1248 closes in 122 s (98 ms each), all inside WindowServer's
calls. "STARLTE GPU BIG": WindowServer creates 34099200-byte buffers (1440 x 2960 x 8: a full-screen 64-bit render
target) again and again. A create allocates wired write-combined memory, flushes and zeroes it and maps it for
the GPU; a close puts every page's cache attribute back and flushes the GPU's address space. This, not the GPU
and not the display path, is why animations, window drags and scrolling are slow.

A closed buffer of ours (over 64 KiB) now goes to a cache of 48 slots as it is: memory, GPU address, GPU mapping.
A worker thread zeroes it; a create of exactly that size takes it (zeroing it itself if the worker has not yet).
Buffers always come out zeroed, so all clients share the cache. Not reused within 3 s, or over sbmcache MiB
(boot-arg, default 160, 0 = off): freed by the worker the old way (sbm_free_buffer). New line every 10 s:
"STARLTE GPU CACHE: creates from the cache N (M zeroed by the caller), not in it N; freed N; no slot N; holding N MiB".
Kernel seq2e = seq2d + 0459.

